{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason","id":1507850,"title":"How would you make pillars for the technocracy/order of reason?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-09T03:55:09-07:00","id":1507850,"title":"How would you make pillars for the technocracy/order of reason?","content":"Or for that matter etherites.<br /> I am OK with each convention having a different set of 4 pillars, but all put together should not be more than 5-6<br /> I imagine for instance that they would lack o have greater difficulty performing the most &quot;mystical&quot; effects of the 9 spheres such as,uhm, summoning of umbrood or creating stuff ex nihilo<br /> <br /> <br /> In the dark ages I am assuming that the Cabal of pure thought has messianic pillars (maybe the ksirafai too) and the rest of them have some interpretation of the hermetic ones albeit with different foundations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 04-09-2023, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T04:33:40-07:00","id":1507857,"title":"","content":"Start with Da:Grimoire. It actually has the baseline for Craftsmasons/proto Etherites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T05:56:22-07:00","id":1507862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason#post1507850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or for that matter etherites.<br /> I am OK with each convention having a different set of 4 pillars, but all put together should not be more than 5-6<br /> I imagine for instance that they would lack o have greater difficulty performing the most &quot;mystical&quot; effects of the 9 spheres such as,uhm, summoning of umbrood or creating stuff ex nihilo</div> </div> </div> </div>These could very well be done ( like other Special Effects of Order of Reason fellows ) through some clockwork machinery, through technical or mechanistic runes and diagrams, through values, story, and experiences - based mentalism, through invocations to reason, intellect, and wisdom, or through alchemical elixir and potions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T07:25:04-07:00","id":1507866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507857#post1507857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Start with Da:Grimoire. It actually has the baseline for Craftsmasons/proto Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had all but forgotten about materia lol.<br /> <br /> What about their spirit effects? What i had in mind was something like the batini's al hajj, The way i see it the Technocrats should see the umbrae as higher dimensions of space, of sorts not unlike how<br /> certain sci-fi stories have it. (i.e a fourth/fifth spatial dimension and the like)<br /> So, entering the Umbra would be Di-Sci 5, just as said pillar. Not sure about which prime-entropy-time effects would be available to them. Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T08:12:35-07:00","id":1507867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507866#post1507866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had all but forgotten about materia lol.<br /> <br /> What about their spirit effects? What i had in mind was something like the batini's al hajj, The way i see it the Technocrats should see the umbrae as higher dimensions of space, of sorts not unlike how<br /> certain sci-fi stories have it. (i.e a fourth/fifth spatial dimension and the like)<br /> So, entering the Umbra would be Di-Sci 5, just as said pillar. Not sure about which prime-entropy-time effects would be available to them. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The view of technocrats on the umbra is as follow<br /> <br /> -the laws of physics are not set, but oppose each other in a sort of cosmic darwinian struggle where the winner is determined by the ammount and structure of information or modeling of said law. The loser still exist appart of the material world, in the umbrae.<br /> <br /> -alongside that, the human brain, being the object with the highest information modeling in the universe, creates and shapes said laws by favoring those they believe in, since by believing, they model them, hence structuring them, making them proeminent over others.<br /> <br /> -howether, models that humans imagine but don't really believe in also appears in the umbra, being modelled into existence, but not enough to appear in the material universe.<br /> <br /> -hence the umbrae are subdimensions of the material universe (and certainly not the other way), collections of imagined things and abandonned laws of the cosmos, and divided by nature and concept.<br /> <br /> -the gauntlet is not truly a barrier, rather, it's a phase of transition that you can only pass by changing your information state.<br /> <br /> -spirits are in reality extradimensional aliens, either born naturally thanks to the discarded laws of the umbra, or modelled into existence directly from human imagination and belief.<br /> <br /> Following all these axioms, the technocrats using dimensional science are using exotic physics and mathematics to shape the state of the gauntlet, disrupt the ephemera of spirits, which is simply umbra's matter, and call them by shaping their informational state to allow their existence in the material world for a time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T09:25:23-07:00","id":1507870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507867#post1507867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The view of technocrats on the umbra is as follow<br /> <br /> -the laws of physics are not set, but oppose each other in a sort of cosmic darwinian struggle where the winner is determined by the ammount and structure of information or modeling of said law. The loser still exist appart of the material world, in the umbrae.<br /> <br /> -alongside that, the human brain, being the object with the highest information modeling in the universe, creates and shapes said laws by favoring those they believe in, since by believing, they model them, hence structuring them, making them proeminent over others.<br /> <br /> -howether, models that humans imagine but don't really believe in also appears in the umbra, being modelled into existence, but not enough to appear in the material universe.<br /> <br /> -hence the umbrae are subdimensions of the material universe (and certainly not the other way), collections of imagined things and abandonned laws of the cosmos, and divided by nature and concept.<br /> <br /> -the gauntlet is not truly a barrier, rather, it's a phase of transition that you can only pass by changing your information state.<br /> <br /> -spirits are in reality extradimensional aliens, either born naturally thanks to the discarded laws of the umbra, or modelled into existence directly from human imagination and belief.<br /> <br /> Following all these axioms, the technocrats using dimensional science are using exotic physics and mathematics to shape the state of the gauntlet, disrupt the ephemera of spirits, which is simply umbra's matter, and call them by shaping their informational state to allow their existence in the material world for a time</div> </div> </div> </div>What source is this from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T09:36:03-07:00","id":1507871,"title":"","content":"The <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b> for <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMRev</b>, published in, what, 2012? It's known as Tychoidean Cosmology, and was fully established by Tychoides in the very early years of the 20th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T12:20:10-07:00","id":1507951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507871#post1507871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b> for <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMRev</b>, published in, what, 2012? It's known as Tychoidean Cosmology, and was fully established by Tychoides in the very early years of the 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I like it, but it's just that, in the context of giving them actual pillars, you have to &quot;cut&quot; some things. I mean, I had 5-6 pillars in mind, so by necessity, i have to think of some weaknesses for them, just as the other fellowships have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T14:55:55-07:00","id":1507961,"title":"","content":"As long as you don't put focus on the Void Engineers, I could really see leaving the Umbra as a weakness of the Technocracy \u2014 though that also potentially excludes the possibility of Black Hats doing the Ghostbusters thing. <br /> <br /> That said, be aware that Pillars are even more versatile than Spheres. The Pillars of the Order of Hermes (the Forma) are close parallels to Forces, Life, Mind, and Prime; and according to DA:Mage Grimoire, the Order of Hermes can use conjunctions of the Mind and Prime equivalents to mess with denizens of the Astral Umbra. <br /> <br /> If I were to create Pillars for the modern Conventions, I'd call them Sciences. I'd start by building three of them around the three Technocratic Sphere variants found in M20: Data, Dimensional Science, and Primal Utility. Maybe rename and expand some of them; for instance:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I could see expanding Primal Utility to Hypereconomics, a Science that covers not just Prime-like Effects but also Entropy-like Effects (at least in the sense of Entropy as manipulation of fortune). This would be a mainstay of the Syndicate. <br /> \u2022 Expand Data to Information Science, and have it include Mind-like Effects as they apply to digital phenomena: e.g., manipulation of senses becomes manipulation of sensors; altering memories becomes messing with stored data; and so on. Both Iteration X and the NWO would like this one; though as I'll address a bit later, it isn't the primary Science of either of them. <br /> \u2022 And incorporate \u201cVoid Correspondence\u201d (a variation of Correspondence that focuses more on its manipulation of space and less on its Sympathetic Links; described in the <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>) into Dimensional Science. This would be the Void Engineers' go-to Science. Also incorporate some elements of Prime and/or Forces into this, with a focus on the luminal aspects of Prime: Dimensional Science should allow for the likes of force fields, laser swords, reactionless drives, phasers, and similar \u201cspace opera\u201d hypertech. In fact, relabel it as \u201cEnergetics\u201d. <br /> <br /> Then add three more Sciences to cover areas that the above miss: <br /> \u2022 the primary Science of Iteration X would be Mechanical Science, which would deal mainly with mechanisms (making them and messing with them). <br /> \u2022 the Progenitors would favor Biological Science, which deals mainly with organisms. In conjunction with Mechanical Science, this allows for cybernetics. <br /> \u2022 the New World Order would focus on Noetic Science, which covers the likes of psychology and sociology. <br /> <br /> So, in summary, six Sciences: <br /> \u2022 Biological Science (Progenitors and ItX)<br /> \u2022 Economic Science (Syndicate)<br /> \u2022 Energetic Science (VEs)<br /> \u2022 Information Science (ItX and NWO)<br /> \u2022 Mechanical Science (ItX and VEs)<br /> \u2022 Noetic Science (NWO and Syndicate)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T15:40:29-07:00","id":1507968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507961#post1507961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you don't put focus on the Void Engineers, I could really see leaving the Umbra as a weakness of the Technocracy \u2014 though that also potentially excludes the possibility of Black Hats doing the Ghostbusters thing.<br /> <br /> That said, be aware that Pillars are even more versatile than Spheres. The Pillars of the Order of Hermes (the Forma) are close parallels to Forces, Life, Mind, and Prime; and according to DA:Mage Grimoire, the Order of Hermes can use conjunctions of the Mind and Prime equivalents to mess with denizens of the Astral Umbra.<br /> <br /> If I were to create Pillars for the modern Conventions, I'd call them Sciences. I'd start by building three of them around the three Technocratic Sphere variants found in M20: Data, Dimensional Science, and Primal Utility. Maybe rename and expand some of them; for instance:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I could see expanding Primal Utility to Hypereconomics, a Science that covers not just Prime-like Effects but also Entropy-like Effects (at least in the sense of Entropy as manipulation of fortune). This would be a mainstay of the Syndicate.<br /> \u2022 Expand Data to Information Science, and have it include Mind-like Effects as they apply to digital phenomena: e.g., manipulation of senses becomes manipulation of sensors; altering memories becomes messing with stored data; and so on. Both Iteration X and the NWO would like this one; though as I'll address a bit later, it isn't the primary Science of either of them.<br /> \u2022 And incorporate \u201cVoid Correspondence\u201d (a variation of Correspondence that focuses more on its manipulation of space and less on its Sympathetic Links; described in the <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>) into Dimensional Science. This would be the Void Engineers' go-to Science. Also incorporate some elements of Prime and/or Forces into this, with a focus on the luminal aspects of Prime: Dimensional Science should allow for the likes of force fields, laser swords, reactionless drives, phasers, and similar \u201cspace opera\u201d hypertech. In fact, relabel it as \u201cEnergetics\u201d.<br /> <br /> Then add three more Sciences to cover areas that the above miss:<br /> \u2022 the primary Science of Iteration X would be Mechanical Science, which would deal mainly with mechanisms (making them and messing with them).<br /> \u2022 the Progenitors would favor Biological Science, which deals mainly with organisms. In conjunction with Mechanical Science, this allows for cybernetics.<br /> \u2022 the New World Order would focus on Noetic Science, which covers the likes of psychology and sociology.<br /> <br /> So, in summary, six Sciences:<br /> \u2022 Biological Science (Progenitors and ItX)<br /> \u2022 Economic Science (Syndicate)<br /> \u2022 Energetic Science (VEs)<br /> \u2022 Information Science (ItX and NWO)<br /> \u2022 Mechanical Science (ItX and VEs)<br /> \u2022 Noetic Science (NWO and Syndicate)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the list a lot. But don't the Void Engineers need Spatial temporal science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T16:55:12-07:00","id":1507978,"title":"","content":"Probably, yes. Fold that into Energetic Science as well. (I was thinking about that after I made my last post.)<br /> <br /> Expanding on this idea, maybe the Technocratic Foundation should be called Logos, from the same root as \u201clogic\u201d. It features an approach to the Sciences that's meticulous and which involves something akin to the Scientific Method, with higher levels of the Foundation aligning with a stronger tendency to think critically. So \u201cLogos\u201d is the Foundation, and the Pillars are the Biological, Economic, Energetic, Information, Mechanical, and Noetic Sciences. Each of the Conventions favors one Science (and for this purpose, I'm including the Virtual Adepts as a Convention): ItX favors Mechanics; NWO favors Noetics; Progenitors favor Biology; Syndicate favors Economics; VAs favor Information; and VEs favor Energetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T17:54:23-07:00","id":1507982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507870#post1507870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What source is this from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The revised edition convention book for void engineers, it is also mention slighly in guide to the technocracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T04:56:18-07:00","id":1508017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1507961#post1507961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you don't put focus on the Void Engineers, I could really see leaving the Umbra as a weakness of the Technocracy \u2014 though that also potentially excludes the possibility of Black Hats doing the Ghostbusters thing.<br /> <br /> That said, be aware that Pillars are even more versatile than Spheres. The Pillars of the Order of Hermes (the Forma) are close parallels to Forces, Life, Mind, and Prime; and according to DA:Mage Grimoire, the Order of Hermes can use conjunctions of the Mind and Prime equivalents to mess with denizens of the Astral Umbra.<br /> <br /> If I were to create Pillars for the modern Conventions, I'd call them Sciences. I'd start by building three of them around the three Technocratic Sphere variants found in M20: Data, Dimensional Science, and Primal Utility. Maybe rename and expand some of them; for instance:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I could see expanding Primal Utility to Hypereconomics, a Science that covers not just Prime-like Effects but also Entropy-like Effects (at least in the sense of Entropy as manipulation of fortune). This would be a mainstay of the Syndicate.<br /> \u2022 Expand Data to Information Science, and have it include Mind-like Effects as they apply to digital phenomena: e.g., manipulation of senses becomes manipulation of sensors; altering memories becomes messing with stored data; and so on. Both Iteration X and the NWO would like this one; though as I'll address a bit later, it isn't the primary Science of either of them.<br /> \u2022 And incorporate \u201cVoid Correspondence\u201d (a variation of Correspondence that focuses more on its manipulation of space and less on its Sympathetic Links; described in the <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>) into Dimensional Science. This would be the Void Engineers' go-to Science. Also incorporate some elements of Prime and/or Forces into this, with a focus on the luminal aspects of Prime: Dimensional Science should allow for the likes of force fields, laser swords, reactionless drives, phasers, and similar \u201cspace opera\u201d hypertech. In fact, relabel it as \u201cEnergetics\u201d.<br /> <br /> Then add three more Sciences to cover areas that the above miss:<br /> \u2022 the primary Science of Iteration X would be Mechanical Science, which would deal mainly with mechanisms (making them and messing with them).<br /> \u2022 the Progenitors would favor Biological Science, which deals mainly with organisms. In conjunction with Mechanical Science, this allows for cybernetics.<br /> \u2022 the New World Order would focus on Noetic Science, which covers the likes of psychology and sociology.<br /> <br /> So, in summary, six Sciences:<br /> \u2022 Biological Science (Progenitors and ItX)<br /> \u2022 Economic Science (Syndicate)<br /> \u2022 Energetic Science (VEs)<br /> \u2022 Information Science (ItX and NWO)<br /> \u2022 Mechanical Science (ItX and VEs)<br /> \u2022 Noetic Science (NWO and Syndicate)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned technomancers as being bad in spirit because, isn't this what all the books say? Virtual adepts revised, Sons of ether revised, and guide to the technocracy seem to agree.<br /> Did the void engineers book retcon it? It's been ages since i read it , but i vividly recall it saying things like &quot; DS can not get you in &quot;x&quot; umbra, or &quot;Tychooidian cosmology does not explain &quot;y&quot; thing, etc&quot;<br /> I have also not read technocracy reloaded.<br /> <br /> Are you sure they should all have the same foundation? I was thinking maybe a different foundation could help differentiate them from each other.<br /> For instance, the sons of Ether and some others (even before they leave) should have &quot;ingenium&quot; or something along those lines. They probably keep the same &quot;sciences&quot; but they manifest with a much more wild look, whereas the VA look, as per canon, like &quot;normal&quot; Enlightened science<br /> <br /> And in regards to the order of reason? Would it fit to have them (minus gabrielites and ksirafai) using the Hermetic forma + materia -(for most of them) primus?<br /> <br /> (I am basing in on the sorcerer's crusade book &quot;Order of Reason&quot; which says that before arete 4 you are not even capable of doing anything that would be considered magickal according to a 1500 pov. So most of Primus would simply not be an option i think, similar to how the DA craftmasons tend to disavow it, but to a much greater degree)<br /> <br /> So, i am thinking Vires, anima, corona, materia, for intiates/mediators/resplendents with primus being mostly a thing for arete 4+ people. The inner labyrinth.<br /> Beyond that, i am not certain if anything else is necessary for that era's Daedalans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T07:05:41-07:00","id":1508028,"title":"","content":"For the Technocracy, they absolutely <i>should</i> have a single Foundation. <b>Book of Secrets</b> talks about how the various Conventions have an easier time of training each other because of their shared Focus. And if the existing Foundations, the Order of Hermes' Modus is a remarkably good fit. <br /> <br /> Your analysis of the early Order of Reason works well for the Artificers, Cosians, and Craftmasons; not the Gabrielites or Ksirafai (which is fine; you've said as much); but also not for the Celestial Masters, High Guild, or Void Seekers.<br /> <br /> The Celestial Masters and Void Seekers need something like Correspondence/Connection: much like the Batini have a Pillar of Mastery of Mind that's similar to, but distinct from, Corona, this Forma should be similar to, but distinct from, the Batini Mastery of Space (Al-Hajj). <br /> <br /> I'd run the High Guild opposite of the Craftmasons: instead of replacing Primus with Materia, replace Vires with Fortuna, a Forma counterpart to the Batini Mastery of Fate. <br /> <br /> The Gabrielites should probably use the Messianic Voices Foundation and Pillars; and I'm thinking that the Ksirafai should use the Batini Foundation and Pillars (Fate, Minds, Space, and Secrets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T07:24:36-07:00","id":1508031,"title":"","content":"The High Guild ends up with Anima, Corona, Fortuna, and Primus: the first has to do with the Art of Desire's focus on self-perfection, specifically perfection of the body; the second deals both with their self-discipline as applied to the mind, and also to their ability to suss out and manipulate other people's wants and desires. The third should be self-evident. And Primus applies to them the same way that Primal Utility applies to the modern Syndicate. <br /> <br /> The Celestial Masters should be able to use their \u201cSpace\u201d Forma in conjunction with something else (I'd say Primus, if they haven't replaced that with Materia) to breach the atmosphere with their skyships and enter the Umbra; similar to how the Dark Ages Order of Hermes uses Primus and Corona to mess with Astral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T08:58:27-07:00","id":1508039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1508031#post1508031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The High Guild ends up with Anima, Corona, Fortuna, and Primus: the first has to do with the Art of Desire's focus on self-perfection, specifically perfection of the body; the second deals both with their self-discipline as applied to the mind, and also to their ability to suss out and manipulate other people's wants and desires. The third should be self-evident. And Primus applies to them the same way that Primal Utility applies to the modern Syndicate.<br /> <br /> The Celestial Masters should be able to use their \u201cSpace\u201d Forma in conjunction with something else (I'd say Primus, if they haven't replaced that with Materia) to breach the atmosphere with their skyships and enter the Umbra; similar to how the Dark Ages Order of Hermes uses Primus and Corona to mess with Astral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, a space forma like the batini's al hajj?? It should be noted that the Hermetic forma, as written, are capable of some space magic. The book even includes an example (vires 4) doing teleportation, so i am not certain if they would have a &quot;direct&quot; space pillar or if it would be, say, a combination of vires 4 primus 4 materia 4 (especially the former 2). In great part because i don't know a lot about the actual Celestial masters lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:58:28-07:00","id":1508074,"title":"","content":"The Celestial Masters are essentially astrologers (and as such ought to have some Time-like ability to make forecasts about the future) who use \u201cskyships\u201d to actually <i>visit</i> the realms of the stars; basically, Mage's version of D&amp;D's Spelljammer concept. By contrast, the Void Seekers are more down-to-Earth explorers who content themselves with visiting mysterious foreign lands. The former focus heavily on exploring the Umbra, while the latter tend to focus more on secrets of geometry and the like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:32:04-07:00","id":1508096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1508074#post1508074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Masters are essentially astrologers (and as such ought to have some Time-like ability to make forecasts about the future) who use \u201cskyships\u201d to actually <i>visit</i> the realms of the stars; basically, Mage's version of D&amp;D's Spelljammer concept. By contrast, the Void Seekers are more down-to-Earth explorers who content themselves with visiting mysterious foreign lands. The former focus heavily on exploring the Umbra, while the latter tend to focus more on secrets of geometry and the like</div> </div> </div> </div> So to sum it up, materia , vires, corona, primus, foftuna, anima <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bbetween the conventions, the archangels for the gabrielites and, hmm something for the ksirafai (thanatoic?) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T20:47:16-07:00","id":1508112,"title":"","content":"The Ksirafai strike me as a surprisingly good fit for the Batini Pillars: primarily minds and secrets; but fate plays a rather large role with them, too. It's only the Foundation that's questionable, as I see it.<br /> <br /> Though the idea of the Ksirafai having Mastery of Space while the Void Seekers and Celestial Masters have to make do with conjunctional effects <i>does</i> rub me the wrong way. It really is <i>that</i> central to the concepts of those latter two Conventions.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> If you're that determines not to let the count go over six Pillars, I'd rather you ditch Fortuna instead of the Space counterpart. Let the High Guild have Anima, Corona, Materia, and Primus, with Materia replacing Vires; let the Void Seekers replace Primus with Materia and Corona with Locus; and let the Celestial Masters replace Corona with Locus but keep Primus. So:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Artificers: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Celestial Masters: Anima, Locus, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Craftmasons: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Cosians: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u2022 High Guild: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u2022 Void Seekers: Anima, Locus, Materia, Vires<br /> <br /> \u2022 Cabal of Pure Thought: Gavri-El, Mikha-El, Repha-El, Uri-El<br /> \u2022 Ksirafai: Al-Anbiya, Al-Fatihah, Al-Hajj, Al-Layl<br /> <br /> Or, if you want each Convention to have a different set of Pillars, have the Artificers replace Corona with Materia instead of replacing Primus; and for the Cosians, replace Vires with Materia:<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u2022 Artificers: Corona, Materia, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Celestial Masters : Anima, Locus, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Craftmasons: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Cosians: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u2022 High Guild: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u2022 Void Seekers: Anima, Locus, Materia<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T23:47:31-07:00","id":1508118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1508074#post1508074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Masters are essentially astrologers (and as such ought to have some Time-like ability to make forecasts about the future) who use \u201cskyships\u201d to actually <i>visit</i> the realms of the stars; basically, Mage's version of D&amp;D's Spelljammer concept. By contrast, the Void Seekers are more down-to-Earth explorers who content themselves with visiting mysterious foreign lands. The former focus heavily on exploring the Umbra, while the latter tend to focus more on secrets of geometry and the like</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very nice and curious to have two Order of Reason Conventions based on exploration, discovery, and geography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T00:44:35-07:00","id":1508124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507850-how-would-you-make-pillars-for-the-technocracy-order-of-reason?p=1508112#post1508112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ksirafai strike me as a surprisingly good fit for the Batini Pillars: primarily minds and secrets; but fate plays a rather large role with them, too. It's only the Foundation that's questionable, as I see it.<br /> <br /> Though the idea of the Ksirafai having Mastery of Space while the Void Seekers and Celestial Masters have to make do with conjunctional effects <i>does</i> rub me the wrong way. It really is <i>that</i> central to the concepts of those latter two Conventions.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> If you're that determines not to let the count go over six Pillars, I'd rather you ditch Fortuna instead of the Space counterpart. Let the High Guild have Anima, Corona, Materia, and Primus, with Materia replacing Vires; let the Void Seekers replace Primus with Materia and Corona with Locus; and let the Celestial Masters replace Corona with Locus but keep Primus. So:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Artificers: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Celestial Masters: Anima, Locus, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Craftmasons: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Cosians: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u2022 High Guild: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u2022 Void Seekers: Anima, Locus, Materia, Vires<br /> <br /> \u2022 Cabal of Pure Thought: Gavri-El, Mikha-El, Repha-El, Uri-El<br /> \u2022 Ksirafai: Al-Anbiya, Al-Fatihah, Al-Hajj, Al-Layl<br /> <br /> Or, if you want each Convention to have a different set of Pillars, have the Artificers replace Corona with Materia instead of replacing Primus; and for the Cosians, replace Vires with Materia:<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u2022 Artificers: Corona, Materia, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Celestial Masters : Anima, Locus, Primus, Vires<br /> \u2022 Craftmasons: Anima, Corona, Materia, Vires<br /> \u2022 Cosians: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u2022 High Guild: Anima, Corona, Materia, Primus<br /> \u2022 Void Seekers: Anima, Locus, Materia<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I based the idea on them having to do it via conjuctional effects on concept that their paradigm was very much half - made back then. For instance, the order of reason book says outright &quot; for some things even the maximi use sorcery because no approximation of science allows them to do so. The implication being, if I am not mistaken, that at this point many of their strongest effects are outright&quot; yes it's sorcery but it's too useful not to do it&quot; or &quot; we can fake it for the outer labyrinth but it's still pretty much sorcery&quot; to, at best &quot;OK here's my scientific theory about it, but unlike the outer labyrinth I can't hide from the truth that it is still fundamentally similar to sorcery&quot;. Or that's how I remember it.<br /> <br /> So I was thinking that not giving them a locus pillar would conceptualise these inherent difficulties, and advantages /temptations of sorcery the era. <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course it is a second edition series of books so it raises the question of how it would have been made today<br /> <br /> That being said, I can see where you are coming from. I will be getting on work for the different concepts to see which one feels better. <br /> <br /> Many thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}